From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 11:48:01 +0930
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] tcl/fpga: read a Lattice ECP5 TraceID

fpga/xilinx-dna.cfg reads the Device DNA a Xilinx part carries; an ECP5
has a 64-bit TraceID in the same role, read with the public UIDCODE_PUB
(0x19) instruction and a 64-bit DR scan, no ISC_ENABLE needed. Only the
low 56 bits are factory programmed; the top 8 come from the bitstream's
TRACE_ID_BINARY preference, so ecp5_read_traceid returns the masked value
and prints both.

Refuses an all-zero or all-one shift, which is an absent or unpowered
chain rather than an identifier. Sequence from Lattice TN1260 and from
ecpdap's read_uid(); the same read is what rpi-hwid performs through a
Cynthion's Apollo controller. Not yet exercised through an OpenOCD
adapter, which the file header says.
---
 tcl/fpga/lattice-ecp5-traceid.cfg | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tcl/fpga/lattice-ecp5-traceid.cfg

diff --git a/tcl/fpga/lattice-ecp5-traceid.cfg b/tcl/fpga/lattice-ecp5-traceid.cfg
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2ec0089
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tcl/fpga/lattice-ecp5-traceid.cfg
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
+
+# Lattice ECP5 TraceID: the die-level unique identifier an ECP5 carries
+# where a Xilinx device has its Device DNA (see fpga/xilinx-dna.cfg).
+#
+# Read with UIDCODE_PUB (0x19) shifted into the 8-bit instruction register
+# and 64 bits shifted out of the data register. It is a public instruction:
+# reading it does not disturb a configured device (ecpdap's read_uid() issues
+# it with no ISC_ENABLE). Of the 64 bits the top 8 are the design's own,
+# set from the bitstream's TRACE_ID_BINARY preference; only the bottom 56
+# bits are programmed at the factory, so anything that names a board after
+# its TraceID should use the masked value this proc returns.
+#
+# Sequence as in Lattice TN1260 (ECP5 sysCONFIG) and the same read as
+# rpi-hwid's fpga.py and ecpdap. Not yet checked against hardware through
+# OpenOCD: the ECP5 used to write this was reached through its Apollo
+# debug controller, not a JTAG adapter OpenOCD drives.
+#
+#   source [find fpga/lattice_ecp5.cfg]
+#   init
+#   ecp5_read_traceid ecp5.tap
+
+proc ecp5_read_traceid {tap} {
+	set UIDCODE_PUB 0x19
+	jtag arp_init
+	irscan $tap $UIDCODE_PUB
+	scan [drscan $tap 32 0 32 0] "%08x %08x" lo hi
+	set raw [expr {($hi << 32) | $lo}]
+	set traceid [expr {$raw & 0x00ffffffffffffff}]
+	if {$traceid == 0 || $traceid == 0x00ffffffffffffff} {
+		error "ecp5_read_traceid: chain shifted all zeros or all ones (device absent or unpowered)"
+	}
+	echo [format "TraceID = 0x%014x (raw 0x%016x)" $traceid $raw]
+	return $traceid
+}
